{"collection":{"version":"1.1","href":"http://images-api.nasa.gov/search?q=Gemini+Titan+liftoff&media_type=image&year_start=1965&year_end=1966&page_size=25","items":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-21090/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1965-03-23T00:00:00Z","description":"S65-21090 (23 March 1965) --- Astronauts Virgil I. Grissom, command pilot; and John W. Young, pilot, wait inside their Gemini-3 spacecraft just after the hatches were closed prior to liftoff. McDonnell Aircraft Corp. technicians can be seen making final adjustments and inspection prior to leaving the white room atop the Titan launch vehicle at Pad 19, Cape Kennedy, Florida. The Gemini-Titan 3 spacecraft is being prepared for launch.","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s65-21090","title":"GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-3 - PRIME CREW - CAPE"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-21090/s65-21090~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":841,"size":136000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-21090/s65-21090~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":420,"size":44000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-21090/s65-21090~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":420,"size":44000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-21090/s65-21090~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1262,"size":280000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-21090/s65-21090~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-56196/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1965-10-23T00:00:00Z","description":"S65-56196 (25 Oct. 1965) --- Astronauts Walter M. Schirra Jr., command pilot; and Thomas P. Stafford, pilot, stand in the white room atop Pad 19 awaiting insertion into their Gemini-6 spacecraft during the prelaunch countdown of the Gemini-Titan-Agena 6 space mission. However, the Gemini-6 liftoff scheduled for Oct. 25 never occurred. The Agena, intended as a rendezvous target vehicle in the mission, failed to achieve orbit. Photo credit: NASA or National Aeronautics and Space Administration","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s65-56196","title":"ASTRONAUT WALTER M. SCHIRRA, JR. - MISC. - INSERTION (PRELAUNCH) - CAPE"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-56196/s65-56196~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":150000,"height":1021},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-56196/s65-56196~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":53000,"height":510},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-56196/s65-56196~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":53000,"height":510},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-56196/s65-56196~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":289000,"height":1532},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-56196/s65-56196~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-21881/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1965-03-22T00:00:00Z","description":"S65-21881 (1965) --- Overall view of the Gemini-Titan 3 on Launch Pad 19, with erector lowered. The GT-3 liftoff was at 9:24 a.m. (EST) on March 23, 1965. A photographer stands at bottom of launch pad with a movie camera.","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s65-21881","title":"GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-3 - ON PAD (OVERALL VIEW) - CAPE"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-21881/s65-21881~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":190000,"height":1241},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-21881/s65-21881~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":46000,"height":620},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-21881/s65-21881~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":46000,"height":620},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-21881/s65-21881~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":453000,"height":1862},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-21881/s65-21881~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-20994/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1965-03-23T00:00:00Z","description":"S65-20994 (23 March 1965) --- A member of the Gemini-Titan 3 prime crew is seen walking onto the gantry ramp at Pad 19 after getting out of a transport van parked at left. The other astronaut is still in the van. The two astronauts then rode the elevator to the top of the launch vehicle to enter the Gemini-3 spacecraft. The GT-3 liftoff was at 9:24 a.m. (EST) on March 23, 1965. The Gemini-3 spacecraft carried astronauts Virgil I. Grissom and John W. Young on three successful orbits of Earth.","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s65-20994","title":"GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-3 - CREW (ENTERS GANTRY) - CAPE"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-20994/s65-20994~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1018,"size":219000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-20994/s65-20994~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":509,"size":71000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-20994/s65-20994~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":509,"size":71000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-20994/s65-20994~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1527,"size":419000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-20994/s65-20994~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-28694/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1965-08-21T00:00:00Z","description":"S65-28694 (21 Aug. 1965) --- The National Aeronautics and Space Administration launched the Gemini-5 spacecraft from Pad 19 at 9 a.m. (EST) Aug. 21, 1965, on a planned eight-day orbital mission. Astronaut L. Gordon Cooper Jr. was the command pilot and astronaut Charles Conrad Jr. was the pilot. A full duration mission will achieve the longest manned spaceflight to date.","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"S65-28694","title":"GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-5 - LIFTOFF - CAPE"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-28694/S65-28694~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":978,"size":117000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-28694/S65-28694~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":489,"size":38000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-28694/S65-28694~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":489,"size":38000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-28694/S65-28694~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1467,"size":245000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-28694/S65-28694~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-29601/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1965-06-02T00:00:00Z","description":"S65-29601 (3 June 1965) --- Distant view of the launch of the Gemini-Titan 4 (GT-4) spacecraft from Pad 19 at 10:16 a.m. (EST) on June 3, 1965. The Gemini IV spacecraft carried astronauts James A. McDivitt, command pilot; and Edward H. White II, pilot, on a four-day, 62-revolution mission that lasted 97 hours and 56 minutes.","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"S65-29601","photographer":"N/A","title":"LIFTOFF - GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-4 - CAPE"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-29601/S65-29601~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":135000,"height":1025},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-29601/S65-29601~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":35000,"height":512},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-29601/S65-29601~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":35000,"height":512},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-29601/S65-29601~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":311000,"height":1537},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-29601/S65-29601~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-61628/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1965-12-04T00:00:00Z","description":"S65-61628 (4 Dec. 1965) --- Gemini-7, carrying astronauts Frank Borman, command pilot, and James A. Lovell Jr., pilot, was successfully launched from Pad 19 at 2:30 p.m., (EST) Dec. 4, 1965. Photo credit: NASA","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"S65-61628","title":"LIFTOFF - GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-7 - CAPE"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-61628/S65-61628~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":612,"size":58000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-61628/S65-61628~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":306,"size":18000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-61628/S65-61628~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":306,"size":18000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-61628/S65-61628~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-61650/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1965-12-04T00:00:00Z","description":"S65-61650 (4 Dec. 1965) --- The Gemini-7 spacecraft, carrying astronauts Frank Borman, command pilot, and James A. Lovell Jr., pilot, was successfully launched by the National Aeronautics and Space Administration  from Pad 19 at 2:30 p.m., (EST) Dec. 4, 1965. The Gemini-7 spacecraft is scheduled for a 14-day mission in space. Photo credit: NASA","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s65-61650","title":"LIFTOFF - GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-7 - CAPE"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-61650/s65-61650~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":591,"size":66000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-61650/s65-61650~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":295,"size":20000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-61650/s65-61650~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":295,"size":20000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-61650/s65-61650~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":886,"size":147000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-61650/s65-61650~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-59970/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-11-11T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-59970 (11 Nov. 1966) --- Gemini-12 spacecraft, carrying astronauts James A. Lovell Jr., command pilot, and Edwin E. Aldrin Jr., pilot, was launched from the Kennedy Space Center's Launch Complex 19 at 3:46 p.m. (EST), Nov. 11, 1966. Photo credit: NASA","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s66-59970","title":"GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-12 - LIFTOFF - CAPE"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-59970/s66-59970~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":651,"size":70000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-59970/s66-59970~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":325,"size":22000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-59970/s66-59970~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":325,"size":22000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-59970/s66-59970~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-59967/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1965-12-12T00:00:00Z","description":"S65-59967 (12 Dec. 1965) --- The National Aeronautics and Space Administration (NASA) attempted to launch Gemini-6 at 9:54 a.m. (EST), Dec. 12, 1965. However, seconds after ignition the first stage engine of the Gemini Launch Vehicle 6 shut down due to a faulty release of a liftoff umbilical plug. Inside the spacecraft were astronauts Walter M. Schirra Jr., command pilot, and Thomas P. Stafford, pilot. Photo credit: NASA or National Aeronautics and Space Administration","keywords":["SPACECRAFT LAUNCHING"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"S65-59967","title":"LIFTOFF - GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-6 - SHUTDOWN - CAPE"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-59967/S65-59967~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":139000,"height":827},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-59967/S65-59967~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":34000,"height":413},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-59967/S65-59967~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":34000,"height":413},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-59967/S65-59967~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":341000,"height":1241},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-59967/S65-59967~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-29636/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1965-06-03T00:00:00Z","description":"S65-29636 (3 June 1965) --- The Gemini-Titan 4 (GT-4) spaceflight launches from Cape Kennedy's Pad 19 at 10:16 a.m. (EST) on June 3, 1965. The GT-4 spacecraft carried astronauts James A. McDivitt, command pilot, and Edward H. White II, pilot, on a four-day, 62-revolution mission. Photo credit: NASA","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"S65-29636","title":"LIFTOFF - GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-4 - CAPE"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-29636/S65-29636~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":598,"size":53000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-29636/S65-29636~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":299,"size":16000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-29636/S65-29636~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":299,"size":16000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-29636/S65-29636~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-59975/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-11-11T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-59975 (11 Nov. 1966) --- Gemini-12 spacecraft, carrying astronauts James A. Lovell Jr., command pilot, and Edwin E. Aldrin Jr., pilot, was launched from the Kennedy Space Center's Launch Complex 19 at 3:46 p.m. (EST), Nov. 11, 1966. Photo credit: NASA","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"S66-59975","title":"GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-12 - LIFTOFF - OFFICIAL - CAPE"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-59975/S66-59975~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1024,"size":98000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-59975/S66-59975~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":512,"size":28000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-59975/S66-59975~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":512,"size":28000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-59975/S66-59975~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1536,"size":233000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-59975/S66-59975~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-53900/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-09-12T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-53900 (12 Sept. 1966) --- The Gemini-11 spacecraft, carrying astronauts Charles Conrad Jr., command pilot, and Richard F. Gordon Jr., pilot, was successfully launched by the National Aeronautics and Space Administration from the Kennedy Space Center's Launch Complex 19 at 9:42 a.m. (EST), Sept. 12, 1966. Photo credit: NASA","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"S66-53900","photographer":"N/A","title":"GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-11 - LIFTOFF - CAPE"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-53900/S66-53900~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1027,"size":120000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-53900/S66-53900~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":513,"size":35000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-53900/S66-53900~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":513,"size":35000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-53900/S66-53900~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1541,"size":261000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-53900/S66-53900~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-29635/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1965-06-03T00:00:00Z","description":"S65-29635 (3 June 1965) --- The Gemini-Titan 4 (GT-4) spaceflight launches from Cape Kennedy's Pad 19 at 10:16 a.m. (EST) on June 3, 1965. The GT-4 spacecraft carried astronauts James A. McDivitt, command pilot, and Edward H. White II, pilot, on a four-day, 62-revolution mission. Photo credit: NASA","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"S65-29635","title":"LIFTOFF - GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-4 - CAPE"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-29635/S65-29635~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":603,"size":71000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-29635/S65-29635~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":301,"size":21000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-29635/S65-29635~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":301,"size":21000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-29635/S65-29635~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image","height":3000,"width":1414,"size":523000}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-34098/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-06-03T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-34098 (3 June 1966) --- The Gemini-9 spacecraft was successfully launched from the Kennedy Space Center's Launch Complex 19 at 8:39 a.m. (EST), June 3, 1966. Photo credit: NASA","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s66-34098","title":"GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-9A - LIFTOFF - CAPE"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-34098/s66-34098~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":594,"size":69000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-34098/s66-34098~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":297,"size":21000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-34098/s66-34098~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":297,"size":21000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-34098/s66-34098~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":891,"size":144000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-34098/s66-34098~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-24465/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-03-16T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-24465 (16 March 1966) --- The Gemini-Titan 8 (GT-8), carrying astronauts Neil A. Armstrong, command pilot, and David R. Scott, pilot, was successfully launched by the National Aeronautics and Space Administration's (NASA) John F. Kennedy Space Center (KSC) at 11:41 a.m. (EST), March 16, 1966. An attempt will be made to rendezvous and dock the Gemini-8 spacecraft with Agena Docking Target Vehicle. Photo credit: NASA","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"S66-24465","title":"LIFTOFF - GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-8 - ATLAS/AGENA - CAPE"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-24465/S66-24465~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":581,"size":59000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-24465/S66-24465~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":290,"size":16000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-24465/S66-24465~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":290,"size":16000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-24465/S66-24465~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-64544/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-11-11T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-64544 (11 Nov. 1966) --- An Agena Target Docking Vehicle atop its Atlas launch vehicle was launched from the Kennedy Space Center's Launch Complex 14 at 2:08 p.m. (EST), Nov. 11, 1966. The Agena served as a rendezvous and docking vehicle for the Gemini-12 spacecraft. Photo credit: NASA","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s66-64544","title":"GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-12 - LIFTOFF - ATLAS/AGENA - CAPE"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-64544/s66-64544~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":611,"size":54000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-64544/s66-64544~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":305,"size":16000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-64544/s66-64544~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":305,"size":16000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-64544/s66-64544~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-50784/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-09-12T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-50784 (12 Sept. 1966) --- An Agena Target Docking Vehicle atop its Atlas launch vehicle was launched from the Kennedy Space Center's Launch Complex 14 at 6:05 a.m., Sept. 12, 1966. The Agena served as a rendezvous and docking vehicle for the Gemini-11 spacecraft. Photo credit: NASA","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"S66-50784","photographer":"N/A","title":"GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-11 - LIFTOFF - ATLAS/AGENA - CAPE"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-50784/S66-50784~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":637,"size":74000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-50784/S66-50784~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":318,"size":23000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-50784/S66-50784~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":318,"size":23000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-50784/S66-50784~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-42762/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-07-18T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-42762 (18 July 1966) --- The Gemini-10 spacecraft is launched from Complex 19 at 5:20 p.m., July 18, 1966. A time exposure creates the illusion of multiple rocker arms. Onboard are astronauts John W. Young, command pilot, and Michael Collins, pilot. Photo credit: NASA","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s66-42762","title":"GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-10 - LIFTOFF - KALEIDOSCOPE EFFECT - CAPE"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-42762/s66-42762~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1007,"size":178000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-42762/s66-42762~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":503,"size":47000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-42762/s66-42762~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":503,"size":47000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-42762/s66-42762~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1511,"size":382000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-42762/s66-42762~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-56161/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1965-10-25T00:00:00Z","description":"S65-56161 (25 Oct. 1965) --- The National Aeronautics and Space Administration launched an Atlas/Agena vehicle at 10 a.m. (EST) on Oct. 25, 1965, from Pad 14. Intended as a rendezvous target vehicle in the Gemini-6 mission, the Agena failed to achieve orbit, and the Gemini-6 mission was scrubbed. Photo credit: NASA or National Aeronautics and Space Administration","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"S65-56161","title":"LIFTOFF - GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-6 - ATLAS/AGENA - CAPE"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-56161/S65-56161~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":235,"size":22000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-56161/S65-56161~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":235,"size":22000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-56161/S65-56161~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-24482/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-03-16T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-24482 (16 March 1966) --- An Agena Target Docking Vehicle atop an Atlas rocket lifts off from Launch Complex 14 at Cape Kennedy at 10 a.m., March 16, 1966 just prior to the Gemini-8 liftoff at nearby Launch Complex 19. The Agena served as a rendezvous and docking vehicle for the Gemini-8 spacecraft. A chase plane leaves a contrail in the background. Photo credit: NASA","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"S66-24482","title":"LIFTOFF - GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-8 - ATLAS/AGENA - CAPE"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-24482/S66-24482~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":173000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-24482/S66-24482~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":47000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-24482/S66-24482~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":47000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-24482/S66-24482~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":387000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-24482/S66-24482~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-42751/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-07-18T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-42751 (18 July 1966) --- An Agena Target Docking Vehicle atop its Atlas launch vehicle was launched from the Kennedy Space Center's Launch Complex 14 at 3:39 p.m. (EST), July 18, 1966. The Gemini-10 liftoff followed the Agena liftoff by 101 minutes. The Agena served as a rendezvous and docking vehicle for the Gemini-10 spacecraft. Photo credit: NASA","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s66-42751","title":"GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-10 - LIFTOFF - ATLAS/AGENA - CAPE"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-42751/s66-42751~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":769,"size":57000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-42751/s66-42751~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":384,"size":17000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-42751/s66-42751~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":384,"size":17000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-42751/s66-42751~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1154,"size":125000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-42751/s66-42751~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-44293/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1965-12-15T00:00:00Z","description":"S65-44293 (15 Dec. 1965) --- Gemini-6, carrying astronauts Walter M. Schirra Jr., command pilot, and Thomas P. Stafford, pilot, was launched by the National Aeronautics and Space Administration?s John F. Kennedy Space Center at 8:37 a.m. (EST), Dec. 15, 1965.  Gemini-6 completed a highly successful rendezvous mission with Gemini-7.","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"S65-44293","title":"LIFTOFF - GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-6 (DISTANT VIEW) - CAPE"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-44293/S65-44293~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":126000,"height":983},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-44293/S65-44293~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":36000,"height":491},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-44293/S65-44293~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":36000,"height":491},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-44293/S65-44293~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":276000,"height":1474},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-44293/S65-44293~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-34610/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-05-17T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-34610 (17 May 1966) --- An Agena Target Vehicle atop its Atlas Launch vehicle is launched from the Kennedy Space Center (KSC) Launch Complex 14 at 10:15 am., May 17, 1966. The Agena was intended as a rendezvous and docking vehicle for the Gemini-9 spacecraft. However, since the Agena failed to achieve orbit, the Gemini-9 mission was postponed. Photo credit: NASA","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s66-34610","title":"LIFTOFF - GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-9A - ATLAS/AGENA - CAPE"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-34610/s66-34610~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":597,"size":58000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-34610/s66-34610~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":298,"size":17000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-34610/s66-34610~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":298,"size":17000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-34610/s66-34610~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":896,"size":129000,"height":1919},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-34610/s66-34610~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-21520/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1965-03-23T00:00:00Z","description":"S65-21520 (23 March 1965) --- Distant view showing the successful launching of the first manned Gemini flight. The Gemini-Titan 3 (GT-3) lifted off Pad 19, at the Kennedy Space Center (KSC) at 9:24 a.m. (EST), March 23, 1965. The Gemini-3 spacecraft \"Molly Brown\" carried astronauts Virgil I. Grissom, command pilot, and John W. Young, pilot, on three successful orbits of Earth.","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"S65-21520","title":"LIFTOFF - GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-3 - DISTANT VIEW - CAPE"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-21520/S65-21520~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":102000,"height":578},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-21520/S65-21520~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":27000,"height":289},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-21520/S65-21520~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":27000,"height":289},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S65-21520/S65-21520~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]}],"metadata":{"total_hits":27},"links":[{"rel":"next","prompt":"Next","href":"http://images-api.nasa.gov/search?q=Gemini+Titan+liftoff&media_type=image&year_start=1965&year_end=1966&page_size=25&page=2"}]}}